Q: How to get task scheduler to run in the early hours? A: <p>The issue lies in your StartBoundary and the interaction with StartWhenAvaliable.</p>
<p>Currently your task is set to 6AM which is exactly when you want to stop running.</p>
<p>how to fix:</p>
<p>1.) Correct the StartBoundary -&gt; change time to 00:00:00</p>
<p>&lt;StartBoundary&gt;2026-04-27T00:00:00&lt;/StartBoundary&gt;</p>
<p>2.) Disable StartWhenAvailable</p>
<p>&lt;StartWhenAvailable&gt;true&lt;/StartWhenAvailable&gt;   --&gt; set this to <strong>false</strong></p>
<p>3.) Add random delay</p>
<p>&lt;RandomDelay&gt;PT1M&lt;/RandomDelay&gt;</p>
<p>4.) Ensure WakeToRun is effective</p>
<p>You have : &lt;WakeToRun&gt;true&lt;/WakeToRun&gt; , what is good, but make sure Windows &quot;Allow Wake Timers&quot; setting is enabled in your Power Profile</p>
<p>So changes will be :</p>
<pre><code>&lt;Triggers&gt;
  &lt;CalendarTrigger&gt;
    &lt;StartBoundary&gt;2026-04-27T00:00:00&lt;/StartBoundary&gt; &lt;Enabled&gt;true&lt;/Enabled&gt;
    &lt;ScheduleByDay&gt;
      &lt;DaysInterval&gt;1&lt;/DaysInterval&gt;
    &lt;/ScheduleByDay&gt;
  &lt;/CalendarTrigger&gt;
&lt;/Triggers&gt;

&lt;Settings&gt;
  &lt;StartWhenAvailable&gt;false&lt;/StartWhenAvailable&gt; &lt;WakeToRun&gt;true&lt;/WakeToRun&gt;
  &lt;/Settings&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Inserting node at the end of a list A: <pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;

struct Node { int data; struct Node* next; };

int main() {
    struct Node *head = NULL, *temp, *newNode;
    int arr[] = {1,2,3}, n = 3;

    for(int i=0;i&lt;n;i++){
        // create node
        newNode = malloc(sizeof(struct Node)); 
        newNode-&gt;data = arr[i]; newNode-&gt;next = NULL;

        // first node
        if(!head) head = newNode;              
        else {
            // go to last                                  
            temp = head; while(temp-&gt;next) temp = temp-&gt;next; 
            // append
            temp-&gt;next = newNode;              
        }
    }

    for(temp=head; temp; temp=temp-&gt;next) printf(&quot;%d -&gt; &quot;, temp-&gt;data);
    printf(&quot;NULL\n&quot;);
}
</code></pre>
